output:
StreamMill event-id deduplication demonstration
health: GET /healthz
  -> HTTP 200 {"service": "streammill", "status": "ok", "version": "0.1.0"}
create deduplicated stream: POST /streams body={"allowed_lateness_ms": 100, "dedup_retention_ms": 5000, "name": "video", "window_ms": 1000}
  -> HTTP 201 {"allowed_lateness_ms": 100, "dedup_retention_ms": 5000, "stream": "video", "window_ms": 1000}
new id aggregates: POST /streams/video/events body={"event_id": "order-7", "timestamp_ms": 100, "value": 5}
  -> HTTP 200 {"dropped": false, "duplicate": false, "stream": "video"}
numeric-equivalent retry: POST /streams/video/events body={"event_id": "order-7", "timestamp_ms": 100, "value": 5.0}
  -> HTTP 200 {"dropped": false, "duplicate": true, "stream": "video"}
conflicting reuse: POST /streams/video/events body={"event_id": "order-7", "timestamp_ms": 100, "value": 6}
  -> HTTP 409 {"error": {"code": "event_id_conflict", "message": "conflicting event_id: order-7"}}
advance lateness boundary: POST /streams/video/watermark body={"watermark_ms": 1000}
  -> HTTP 200 {"finalized": [], "stream": "video", "watermark_ms": 1000}
retained retry wins over lateness: POST /streams/video/events body={"event_id": "order-7", "timestamp_ms": 100, "value": 5}
  -> HTTP 200 {"dropped": false, "duplicate": true, "stream": "video"}
unseen late id is dropped: POST /streams/video/events body={"event_id": "never-seen", "timestamp_ms": 200, "value": 9}
  -> HTTP 200 {"dropped": true, "duplicate": false, "stream": "video"}
close window: POST /streams/video/watermark body={"watermark_ms": 1100}
  -> HTTP 200 {"finalized": [{"count": 1, "stream": "video", "sum": 5, "window_end_ms": 1000, "window_start_ms": 0}], "stream": "video", "watermark_ms": 1100}
final results: GET /streams/video/results
  -> HTTP 200 {"results": [{"count": 1, "stream": "video", "sum": 5, "window_end_ms": 1000, "window_start_ms": 0}], "stream": "video"}
Observed: only the first accepted id changed the window; retry and conflict did not.
